Bidirectional Audio Breakdown

    AudioRecorder.kt (Input Stream: Client → Model):

        Role: Captures live audio from the device microphone.

        Format: Converts browser audio buffer into 16-bit PCM little-endian mono audio at a 16kHz sample rate.

        Transmission: Emits PCM chunks via onAudioChunk callback to be base64-encoded and sent over the WebSocket connection to Gemini.

    AudioPlayer.kt (Output Stream: Model → Client):

        Role: Plays back incoming audio chunks returned by the model in real time.

        Format: Receives raw 16-bit PCM little-endian audio at a 24kHz sample rate from the model stream.

        Playback: Converts integer PCM samples into normalized 32-bit floats and schedules them sequentially in Web Audio API to prevent gaps or audio cracking.

