Production Security Mechanics

    WebAuthn Passkey Prompt: Uses navigator.credentials.get with userVerification: "required". This forces the operating system and browser to invoke Touch ID, Face ID, Windows Hello, or Android Fingerprint/Screen Lock.

    Hardware Availability Check: Calls PublicKeyCredential.isUserVerifyingPlatformAuthenticatorAvailable() before attempting invocation to gracefully return an error if the user lacks biometric hardware.

    Explicit Failure Handling: Captures user cancellations (NotAllowedError), timeouts, and missing hardware, passing exact diagnostic strings to onError so your UI can fall back to PIN or password login rather than silently auto-succeeding.

