Key Production Changes

    Passkey Registration (navigator.credentials.create): Replaces the hardcoded Pair("wasm_cred_id", "wasm_pub_key") with WebAuthn API invocation. It returns Base64-encoded rawId and attestationObject values from biometric or platform authenticators.  

    Wallet Connection (eth_requestAccounts): Replaces the hardcoded "wasm-coinbase-wallet" string with an EIP-1193 JSON-RPC request to window.coinbaseWalletExtension or window.ethereum to retrieve the authenticated public EVM wallet address.  

    Async Suspension: Wraps asynchronous browser Promises inside Kotlin's suspendCancellableCoroutine, resuming execution on success or throwing an exception on user cancellation or failure.

Findings & Security Analysis

1. Hardcoded Credentials & Global State Leakage (firebase-auth.js)

    Hardcoded Dummy Keys: The Firebase configuration contains placeholder strings (dummy_api_key_for_local_build, 1:123456789012...). All authentication requests will fail in production.  

    Global Scope Contamination: Storing confirmationResult and recaptchaVerifier on the window object risks memory leaks, state collision across multiple login attempts, and variable overwriting.  

2. Missing DOM Container (index.html)

    Broken Phone Auth: firebase-auth.js instantiates RecaptchaVerifier targeting 'recaptcha-container', but index.html has an empty <body> element. Attempting phone verification will throw a DOM element null reference exception.  

3. Dead-End Placeholder (MetaWearablesPage.kt)

    Incomplete Web Target: The page renders a static text box stating glasses are unsupported on Web. The web interface should provide a full management dashboard for device status, pairing controls, hands-free checkout triggers, and WebRTC camera streaming preview.  

