An audit of these wardrobe feature files identified color contrast defects, GlobalScope coroutine leaks, unpopulated local state, and dead wildcard imports.  

Code Audit Findings

    Color Contrast Defects (WardrobeStylingEngineSection.kt): The parent Surface used color = MaterialTheme.colorScheme.primary, while child elements rendered primary text on top of primary backgrounds and onSurface text on primary containers. In the fit cards, fit.season text also rendered primary on primary.  

    GlobalScope Coroutine Anti-Pattern (WardrobeViewPage.kt): handleAddPhoto invoked kotlinx.coroutines.GlobalScope.launch { ... }. In Compose, coroutines should be tied to structured lifecycles using rememberCoroutineScope() to avoid memory and exception leaks.  

    Unpopulated Outfit State (WardrobeViewPage.kt): curatedFits was initialized as an empty list and never updated when fetching outfits in LaunchedEffect(activeSeason).  

    Inline Qualified References & Dead Imports: WardrobeViewPage.kt contained fully qualified references (such as androidx.compose.ui.platform.LocalLayoutDirection.current) and unused wildcard imports.  

